A||||1||K9||Where dose this pipe go?
Z||000000||K9||09-03-99||06:08 AM||||while changing the spark plug wires in my 85 GT, I came accross a pipe about 1" dimater. The pipe is located by the inner valve cover (towards the front of the car) and is not hooked to anything. The pipe has an open end and looks like it should be pluged into something. I can't tell where it is to plug into.  The pipe leads in towards the air cleaner. Can anyone help? Note: It is not the metalpipe that goes from the valve cover to the intake.
Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-03-99||08:32 AM||||the pipe that you see...is that pretty long almost all the way to the air filter housing??? if so don't worry about it...that pipe that you see used to be the old breather for your PCV valve cover...When Pontiac did the "Recall" they change everything and that got eliminated...
